# 1. CRITICAL CUSTOMER FEEDBACK

Following a real customer demonstration, three major product changes have been approved.

## CHANGE 1 — Reuse the Student dossier interface

The reviewer should inspect the SAME dossier presentation that the Student uses.

Do not maintain two independently designed dossier interfaces.

Create a reusable dossier presentation foundation that supports different role-based capabilities.

## CHANGE 2 — Forward the School's selected application list ONE TIME

At School level, reviewers perform preliminary assessment as usual.

After the School finishes preparing its selected applications, it must:

1. Review the complete selected list.
2. Attach the official School decision document.
3. Confirm the batch.
4. Forward the entire selected list to City exactly once per authorized School Review Unit and award season.

For the University of Da Nang, ONE shared forwarding batch covers ALL eight configured member institutions.

## CHANGE 3 — Simplify internal City and Committee review

The customer does not want complex ambiguous-case workflows, separate Resolution Hub processing, artificial escalation steps, or fictional Committee meeting workflows.

Keep the real review functions.

Remove unnecessary workflow complexity.

The outcome must be a more intuitive, faster, calmer application for experienced reviewers.

