# 20. REPORTING FORMAT

After each phase provide:

1. Phase name and objective.
2. Current source baseline.
3. Real changes implemented.
4. Exact frontend files changed.
5. Exact backend files changed.
6. Prisma changes, if any.
7. API/DTO changes.
8. Authorization behavior.
9. Demo verification.
10. Test command results.
11. Browser verification evidence.
12. Known blockers.
13. Actual readiness status.
14. Recommended next phase.

Use:

PASS / PARTIAL / BLOCKED.

Do not use PASS if major implementation is missing or not verified.

Clearly distinguish:

- Coded.
- Unit tested.
- HTTP tested.
- Browser verified.
- Database integration verified.
- Production ready.

These are not equivalent.

